  "question": {
    "text": "An automobile, travelling at $40 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$, can be stopped at a distance of $40 \\mathrm{~m}$ by applying brakes. If the same automobile is travelling at $80 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$, the minimum stopping distance, in metres, is (assume no skidding)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
